From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:13:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommax: pcs-qca-uniphy: re-resolve the link on a USXGMII
 rate change

An AQR113C can report its copper link over MDIO before it writes the
new rate into the USXGMII code word, which carries 10G while the copper
link is down. phylink reads the speed only when the link comes up, so
the MAC stays at 10G. On an RT-AX89X with a 1G partner on the AQR113C
port this happened in 3 of 20 link-ups, and the port passed no traffic.

Report a rate change in the code word as a link drop, so that phylink
resolves the link again at the new rate. With this change all 20
link-ups ended at 1G; 9 came up at 10G first and were re-resolved
within a second.

Fixes: 05c180511dda ("qualcommax: add UNIPHY PCS driver")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/25829
Signed-off-by: Robert Marko <robimarko@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 59f295f58fd73b105395b36dc4093458185f7176)
---
 .../qualcommax/files/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.c | 11 +++++++++++
 .../files/include/linux/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.h          |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/files/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.c b/target/linux/qualcommax/files/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.c
index 91c34c5394..0e8b605353 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/files/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.c
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/files/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.c
@@ -395,6 +395,17 @@ static void qca_uniphy_pcs_get_state_usxgmii(struct qca_uniphy *uniphy,
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/* The PHY can report its link before it writes the new rate into
+	 * the code word, and phylink takes the speed only when the link
+	 * comes up. Report a rate change as a link drop so that phylink
+	 * resolves the link again at the new rate.
+	 */
+	if (state->speed != uniphy->usxgmii_speed) {
+		uniphy->usxgmii_speed = state->speed;
+		state->link = false;
+		return;
+	}
+
 	state->duplex = DUPLEX_FULL;
 }
 
diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/files/include/linux/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.h b/target/linux/qualcommax/files/include/linux/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.h
index a540416a23..87f5698a89 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/files/include/linux/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.h
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/files/include/linux/pcs/pcs-qca-uniphy.h
@@ -146,6 +146,8 @@ struct qca_uniphy {
 	struct clk_bulk_data *clks;
 	int num_clks;
 	struct qca_uniphy_pcs port_pcs[QCA_UNIPHY_CHANNELS];
+	/* USXGMII rate the code word carried at the last read */
+	int usxgmii_speed;
 	struct qca_uniphy_clk rx_clk;
 	struct qca_uniphy_clk tx_clk;
 	struct qca_uniphy_clk ref_clk;
